    "title": "Subtronics' Coachella Debut Marks New Era at Sahara Tent - Coachella Today",
    "text": "Got story updates? Submit your updates here. ›Subtronics' Coachella debut promises to be a visually stunning, high-energy performance that blends the artist's signature bass-driven sound with a more nuanced, melodic approach.Coachella TodaySubtronics, the stage name of artist Jesse Kardon, is set to make his Coachella debut on Sunday, April 12. After nearly a decade of building his project, Kardon is excited to bring his signature high-intensity, bass-driven sound to the Sahara Tent, while also showcasing a more nuanced, melodic side of his music. Kardon has designed a brand new, custom stage production for the occasion, aiming to create an 'audio-visual roller coaster' that will appeal to both longtime fans and first-time listeners. Why it matters Subtronics' Coachella debut marks a significant milestone for the independent artist, who has steadily grown his project over the years. His appearance at the iconic music festival represents a coming-of-age moment, as Kardon looks to expand the sonic universe of Subtronics and connect with a wider audience. The details For his Coachella set, Kardon has designed a completely new stage production, fabricated from scratch, that will feature a balance of the high-intensity, bass-driven elements Subtronics is known for, as well as more melodic and introspective moments. Kardon wants to create an experience that appeals to both longtime fans and first-time listeners, with familiar tracks mixed in with unreleased material and new edits. Subtronics will make his Coachella debut on Sunday, April 12, 2026.Kardon has been building the Subtronics project for nearly a decade. The players SubtronicsThe stage name of artist Jesse Kardon, known for his high-intensity, bass-driven electronic music.CoachellaThe iconic music festival held annually in Indio, California. Got photos? Submit your photos here. › What they’re saying “Everything about this is completely beyond my wildest dreams. When I started, I just wanted to learn how to make music, I didn't have expectations of playing something like Coachella. So now, having opportunities like this, it honestly feels like I'm in a coma dream or something. Like a fantasy version of what it would be like if you won the lottery.”— Jesse Kardon, Artist (Subtronics)“It really feels like a coming-out party for this new, more grown-up, more nuanced side of the project. It's a way of showing where things are heading. But on a personal level, just being able to say I played Coachella, it's insane. It's something I'll tell my kids about one day.”— Jesse Kardon, Artist (Subtronics) What’s next Subtronics' Coachella performance on April 12, 2026 will be a highly anticipated moment, marking a new era for the artist and his evolving sound. The takeaway Subtronics' Coachella debut showcases the artist's ability to balance his signature high-intensity, bass-driven style with more melodic and introspective elements, creating a dynamic performance that aims to connect with both longtime fans and new listeners.",
